{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_service_layer", "label": "Service layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What most consumers should use: adds input validation, structured logging via ILogger<T>, result normalization, and the documented auto-retry policy on top of the client layer."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_client_layer", "label": "Client layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Thin, single-attempt translations to/from the COM API (or CLI for the two COM-gap features), exposed so callers who want full control over retry behavior can bypass the service layer."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_activation_layer", "label": "Activation layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Internal layer that creates every COM object through one resilient activation chain so all COM objects share a single activation context."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_ipackagemanagementservice", "label": "IPackageManagementService", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_ipackagesourceservice", "label": "IPackageSourceService", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_iwingetclient", "label": "IWinGetClient", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_iwingetsourceclient", "label": "IWinGetSourceClient", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_iwingetcliclient", "label": "IWinGetCliClient", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Isolates the only two CLI-backed features (pins, export/import) behind one interface so the winget.exe dependency cannot spread into the rest of the library."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_wingetfactory", "label": "WinGetFactory (internal)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_activation_chain", "label": "Resilient COM activation chain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three ordered modes \u2014 WinRT projection activation (new PackageManager()), CoCreateInstance with CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER against winget-cli's out-of-proc production CLSIDs, then CoCreateInstance with CLSCTX_ALLOW_LOWER_TRUST_REGISTRATION (the documented mitigation for elevated hosts, as used by the WinGet PowerShell module and UniGetUI). The first success is cached so every COM object shares one activation context; if all three fail, WinGetUnavailableException is thrown."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_composite_catalogs", "label": "Composite catalogs everywhere", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#composite-catalogs-everywhere", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every lookup merges remote sources with local install state via CreateCompositePackageCatalog, the architecturally correct approach and what winget itself does, so installed state correlates with available versions; get-by-id and mutating operations need the exact CatalogPackage WinGet associates with the installed app for upgrade/uninstall/repair to work at all."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_unreachable_source_resilience", "label": "Unreachable-source resilience", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#composite-catalogs-everywhere", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If the composite catalog fails to connect, each source is probed individually and the composite is rebuilt from the reachable subset rather than failing the whole call."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_selectors_or_filters_and", "label": "Selectors are OR'd, Filters are AND'd", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#verified-com-api-findings", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verified by running the API: FindPackagesOptions.Selectors are OR'd while Filters are AND'd, so multi-field search (name or id or moniker or tag) is a single call carrying multiple Selectors."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_indexed_for_loop_rule", "label": "Indexed for-loops over CsWinRT collections", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#verified-com-api-findings", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Enumerating a CsWinRT-projected IReadOnlyList<T> via foreach/LINQ throws InvalidCastException in interop 1.29.280, so all collection traversal uses indexed for loops and must not be 'simplified'."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_extendederrorcode_is_exception", "label": "ExtendedErrorCode is an Exception, not an int", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#verified-com-api-findings", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "InstallResult.ExtendedErrorCode is typed as an Exception, so the HRESULT must be read from its .HResult property."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_separate_progress_mappers", "label": "Separate progress mappers per operation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#verified-com-api-findings", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "InstallProgress and UninstallProgress are different WinRT structs with public fields, so a single shared mapper is impossible."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_wingetunavailableexception", "label": "WinGetUnavailableException", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A typed exception so a raw COMException never escapes when WinGet is missing, too old, or COM activation is blocked."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_wingeterrorcodes", "label": "WinGetErrorCodes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#error-codes", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exposes well-known APPINSTALLER_CLI_ERROR_* HRESULTs already unchecked-cast to int so they compare directly against ExtendedErrorCode."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_hosting_caveats", "label": "Hosting caveats (elevation, SYSTEM, concurrency)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#hosting-caveats", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "COM activation under LocalSystem and winget's scope behavior in profile-less contexts are not yet validated by the test suite, so service hosting is an open item; the library also adds no global lock because WinGet already serializes some source operations internally."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_winget_return_codes_doc", "label": "winget-cli return-code documentation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#error-codes", "source_url": "https://github.com/microsoft/winget-cli/blob/master/doc/windows/package-manager/winget/returnCodes.md", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_service_layer", "target": "docs_architecture_ipackagemanagementservice", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_service_layer", "target": "docs_architecture_ipackagesourceservice", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_client_layer", "target": "docs_architecture_iwingetclient", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": "docs/architecture.md#layers", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_client_layer", "target": "docs_architecture_iwingetsourceclient", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_loca